course: dictionary
lesson: 8537
title: A place word: sawmill
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sawmill is a noun, a name for a place. Split the word into its two parts: a saw cuts wood, and a mill is a place where something is made or worked. Put them together and you get a factory where logs are cut into planks and boards by machine saws.
explain: The sentence gives you a clue: «A bagless vacuum spins the air like a whirlwind, flinging dust to the sides of the bin where it drops; the idea came from big dust separators in sawmills.» The sentence says sawmills have big machines that catch dust, so they are busy workplaces, not quiet ones.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «the idea came from big dust separators in factories where logs are cut into planks». It still makes sense, so your meaning fits. Sawmills is the plural, and you can say «work at the sawmill» or «an old sawmill».
fact: A sawmill is a factory or building where logs are cut into planks and boards by machine saws.
fact: Sawmills grew up beside rivers in Canada, New Zealand, Australia and the US, and at first they used water power.
fact: Wood for houses and furniture comes from sawmills.
fact: Sawmills are dangerous places with big blades, so workers must follow safety rules.
fact: The phrase «work at the sawmill» means having a job in that factory.
exercise: What is a sawmill? | *A factory where logs are cut into planks by machine saws | A shop that sells furniture | A type of tree | A kind of boat used on rivers
exercise: Where does wood for houses and furniture come from? | A bakery | A paint shop | *A sawmill | A tree in the park
exercise: Sawmills are dangerous places with big blades. Find and copy the word that tells you they are risky. | places | sawmills | *dangerous | blades
test: «She got a job at the sawmill.» What does sawmill mean? | A kind of ship | *A factory where logs are cut into planks | A river with a waterfall | A school for woodwork
test: Which sentence uses sawmills correctly? | Please sawmill the door. | *Wood for the new furniture came from sawmills. | Sawmills are a kind of cloud | The children sawmilled their lunch
exam: Using the clue «big dust separators in sawmills», what kind of place is a sawmill? | A sunny garden | A quiet library | *A busy workplace full of big machines | A place for sleeping
